  "description": "I want to build a comprehensive machine learning system that can analyze medical imaging data to detect early signs of diabetic retinopathy in patients across multiple hospitals and clinical settings worldwide. The system should process retinal fundus photographs captured using different camera models and under varying clinical conditions, and classify them into different stages of the disease, ranging from no retinopathy through mild non-proliferative diabetic retinopathy, moderate non-proliferative diabetic retinopathy, severe non-proliferative diabetic retinopathy, and finally proliferative diabetic retinopathy. I need a model that can achieve high accuracy while being interpretable for clinical use, providing explanations for its predictions so that ophthalmologists can understand and trust the system. The dataset should include labeled images from diverse patient populations with varying image quality and lighting conditions to ensure robustness and generalizability across different clinical environments."
